      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n---\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, Error\u003e GetBootVersion(const UsbDevice\u0026 device,\n                                          DeviceMode current_mode) {\n  const size_t expected_size \u003d (current_mode \u003d\u003d DeviceMode::kBootloader)\n                                   ? kBootVersionMax\n                                   : kRomVersionMax;\n\n  // Allocate the maximum possible size on the stack and zero-initialize it.\n  std::array\u003cuint8_t, std::max(kBootVersionMax, kRomVersionMax)\u003e data{};\n  \n  // Create a bounded view that acts as the single source of truth.\n  auto buffer \u003d std::span(data).first(expected_size);\n\n  if (const auto res \u003d ReceiveBulkDataIn(\n          device,\n          CmdFormat{.opcode \u003d Opcode::kReadInfo, .subcmd \u003d Subcmd::kReadData},\n          buffer, kGenericInfoTimeout);\n      !res) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Failed to read version info\");\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  // Safely construct the string. If \u0027\\0\u0027 is not found, it stops exactly at buffer.end().\n  const std::string version(buffer.begin(), std::ranges::find(buffer, \u0027\\0\u0027));\n  \n  FT_LOGI(\"Boot version: {}\", version);\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n### Key Improvements\n\n* **Single Source of Truth (`buffer`):** We slice the `std::array` into a `std::span` immediately. Both the USB read and the null-terminator search now operate *only* on this bounded `buffer`. This directly resolves the buffer-searching bug we identified earlier.\n* **One-Liner String Parsing:** `std::string(buffer.begin(), std::ranges::find(buffer, \u0027\\0\u0027))` cleanly handles both scenarios. If a null terminator exists, it truncates the string there. If the MCU returns a string without a null terminator, `std::ranges::find` returns `buffer.end()`, and the string safely copies the exact byte length without reading out of bounds.\n* **Inline Struct Instantiation:** Because the `CmdFormat` struct is only used once, defining it directly inside the `ReceiveBulkDataIn` call removes unnecessary local variables and keeps the function\u0027s vertical footprint small.\n* **Scoped Error Handling:** Using the C++17 `if` statement with an initializer (`if (const auto res \u003d ...; !res)`) limits the scope of the `res` variable strictly to the error-handling block, preventing accidental reuse later in the function.",
